---
/**
 * FAQ for the Germany Product page.
 * Uses _shared/FaqRb.astro for accordion structure, schema markup, and styling.
 * Questions and answers updated for Germany B2B e-invoicing mandate & ViDA.
 */
import FaqRb from "../_shared/FaqRb.astro";
import type { FaqItem } from "../_shared/FaqRb.astro";

const items: FaqItem[] = [
  {
    q: "What are the leading e-invoicing suites that support both PDF and structured formats?",
    a: "Germany works with two invoice format families. ZUGFeRD is the hybrid one, a readable PDF carrying EN 16931 XML inside it, while XRechnung and Peppol BIS 3.0 are pure structured XML. A suite worth choosing reads and writes all three, validates against the schema before an invoice leaves your system, and stores the structured copy for archival. ClearTax does all of this on one platform.",
  },
  {
    q: "What are the top-rated Peppol e-invoicing services supporting global formats?",
    a: "Peppol only moves invoices through certified Access Points, so your provider has to be a registered one. ClearTax is a registered Peppol Access Point and complies with the BIS Billing 3.0 standard. It also supports XRechnung, ZUGFeRD and local formats across 50+ markets, which starts to matter the moment you invoice across borders. Confirm the Access Point registration first when you compare options.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I choose the right e-invoicing software for my business in Germany?",
    a: "You need software that can generate, send, receive, validate and archive EN 16931-compliant invoices in formats such as XRechnung, ZUGFeRD and Peppol BIS. This can be your ERP's own e-invoicing capability or a third-party e-invoicing provider integrated with your ERP or accounting system. Make sure it automates validation, reduces manual entry and offers secure long-term archiving. A reliable solution should simplify compliance and reduce operational effort.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which are the best e-invoicing solutions for multinational companies in Europe?",
    a: "For a multinational, the real question is whether one platform covers every market you trade in, or whether you end up running a fresh project country by country. ClearTax uses a single API across 50+ countries, with country-level configuration per mandate and one dashboard for visibility. It is VeR-listed in Germany, a registered Peppol Access Point, and already built for EU ViDA from 2030. Shortlist it against tax consultants, local players and global EDI vendors, then compare on coverage.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which cloud ERP platforms support complex manufacturing operations and comply with German tax and e-invoicing requirements?",
    a: "Cloud ERPs made for complex manufacturing, like SAP S/4HANA Cloud, Oracle (Fusion and NetSuite) and Microsoft Dynamics 365, handle the production and finance side well. On their own they rarely cover German e-invoicing from start to finish. Structured format conversion, schema validation, transmission over Peppol or EDI and 8-year GoBD archival usually need a dedicated compliance layer. ClearTax connects to all three through pre-built connectors and takes care of that part.",
  },
  {
    q: "What are the advantages of using e-Invoicing software?",
    a: "It reduces manual entry, errors, and processing time; improves audit trails; supports automated matching and approvals; speeds dispute resolution; and ensures compliance. It also centralizes monitoring and helps meet archiving and reporting needs efficiently.",
  },
  {
    q: "What are the main requirements of the Germany e-Invoicing mandate?",
    a: "All German businesses must be able to receive structured e-invoices from 2025. Companies with revenue above 800,000 euros must issue e-invoices from 2027. By 2028, e-invoice issuance becomes mandatory for all companies. Structured invoices must follow EN 16931 formatting rules and be exchanged digitally.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do businesses need to register on a government system to send e-invoices in Germany?",
    a: "No registration is required. Germany follows a decentralised model. Businesses are responsible for ensuring their invoices meet EN 16931 standards and are exchanged through approved digital channels such as Peppol, EDI or compliant e-Invoicing software. There is no clearance or central approval portal.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I create an e-invoice myself?",
    a: "You can create one provided you use a software that can create an invoice as per the German requirements for an E-Rechnung, and the structured-data requirements and applicable EN 16931 syntax/profile. Tools like Excel can store invoice data but can't produce a compliant e-invoice on their own; you'd still need software or middleware to convert that data into XRechnung or ZUGFeRD and validate it.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can a PDF be converted into an e-invoice?",
    a: "A normal PDF is not itself an E-Rechnung under Germany's structured e-invoicing rules. A valid structured e-invoice must contain the required machine-readable data. A PDF can serve as the visual component of a qualifying hybrid format such as ZUGFeRD, which includes structured XML data. Simply converting or renaming a PDF does not make it a compliant e-invoice.",
  },
  {
    q: "What do I need to receive an e-invoice?",
    a: "Since 1 January 2025, businesses in Germany have needed to be able to receive e-invoices. You need a system that can accept and process EN 16931 invoices, such as ERP/AP automation, accounting software with e-invoice import, or an e-invoicing provider portal. Enterprise businesses generally also need a process to identify, validate, route, process and archive incoming e-invoices. ClearTax can centralise these receiving workflows and connect them with your ERP or AP processes.",
  },
  {
    q: "How can I switch to e-invoicing?",
    a: "Start with your existing invoice process rather than replacing it from scratch. Map your current ERP and billing landscape, identify applicable Germany transactions, choose your formats and exchange channels, integrate your ERP, make sure incoming e-invoices can be received, validated and routed, and set up archiving.",
  },
];
---

<FaqRb items={items} subtitle="" />
